From 9ee1dee924f4ba8cd7c223c78347fd273aa35c6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:57:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 158/180] cmake: a standalone build gets Embree again

Upstream 30201123 (in release/5.3) switched the sources from
WITH_CYCLES_EMBREE to Blender's WITH_EMBREE, which only Blender's build
sets. A standalone build then compiled without WITH_EMBREE: the CPU device
offered only BVH2, slower, and everything resting on Embree (ray masks,
per-query user geometry callbacks) silently did nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/cmake/external_libs.cmake | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cmake/external_libs.cmake b/src/cmake/external_libs.cmake
index 5b5ae357..b75704e2 100644
--- a/src/cmake/external_libs.cmake
+++ b/src/cmake/external_libs.cmake
@@ -508,6 +508,11 @@ if(WITH_CYCLES_EMBREE)
   else()
     add_bundled_libraries(embree/lib)
   endif()
+
+  # The sources test Blender's WITH_EMBREE since upstream 30201123 (Aug 2026), which only
+  # Blender's build defines: a standalone build silently lost Embree, the CPU fell back to
+  # BVH2. Set it here.
+  set(WITH_EMBREE ON)
 endif()
 
 
